   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*A cambio de* (in exchange for) names what one party gives, requires, or offers in a transaction or agreement -- essential for describing conditional deals like loans with strings attached. It's followed by a noun phrase or que + subjunctive. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *se* with a verb from B1 Unit 6. It leaves out who does the action, which is useful when a text speaks of cuts, taxes and agreements and the decision-makers stay in the background. With no noun the verb stays singular; with a noun the verb agrees with it."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "El FMI ofrecía nuevos préstamos a cambio de que los gobiernos aceptaran una serie de condiciones económicas.",
