       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "*En detrimento de* always names the loser in a trade-off -- pair it naturally with a phrase describing who benefits (*a favor de* or *en beneficio de*) when a reading wants to make the full trade-off explicit."
+      "content": "*Cuanto* does not change before a verb, and *más* or *menos* can start either part: *cuanto menos ganaban, más difícil era vivir*. Use *mejor* or *peor*, not *más bueno* or *más malo*. After *a medida que* the verb is in the indicative when you describe what happened."
